{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b. Describing rather than refusing is the right boundary: unknown body keys are intentionally open, while an immediate projection note can expose how the governed fold read the admitted act. The result must, however, be true for every durable event shape.\n\n1. resolves() searches only projection.Statements. Ratify and supersede events are durable events in projection.Decisions/Acts but are not statements; the fold explicitly supports superseding a supersession. A valid target or rests_on citation naming such an act is therefore falsely returned as unresolved. Resolve existence from projection.Decisions, which has exactly one row per durable record, and pin both a valid act target and a valid act citation.\n\n2. When act.Kind is report and no projected Review is found, the code always says body.verdict was not set. That is false for an ineffective report which did set body.verdict but had no valid promise or failed another fold precondition. The live log contains exactly this shape: report 97c96c1f7095631a0cd241f69e64db018d21031b has body.verdict=changes-requested, decision ineffective (“report has no promise”), and no Review row. Base the explanation on the submitted body plus the decision; never infer a missing field merely from absence of a Review.\n\n3. If the post-append Snapshot fails, state gets a kind warning but ratify/supersede return no projected disclosure at all. The documentation promises that the result carries projected notes. Return an explicit projected-unavailable diagnostic for every verb rather than silently dropping the very check this change adds.\n\n4. Candidate artifact 5fa6ba08 has succession_unrecorded at request/mcp-projection-notes; retire live predecessor 022cc912 for f904524f with the successor as causal basis. The changed docs/reference/mcp/state.md also still rests on old behavior artifacts, including stale comma-path d314fad and whole-repository 15390758, but not this new projected-result behavior. Re-anchor the page to the live exact behavior artifact when publishing the repaired head.\n\nFocused projection-note tests and go vet pass; git diff --check is clean; exact worktree is clean; main merges cleanly at tree cecd486c04cbf56e70208613c0acd0cfc0825eac. The present unit tests miss findings 1–3 because they exercise only statement IDs, a no-verdict effective report, and direct projectionNotes calls rather than the post-submit boundary.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5fa6ba087e3b425c0b4888094a759be13e292011","head":"287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b","verdict":"changes-requested"}}